+
+---
+
+## 19. Production Local Authentication Extension
+
+### Approved requirement
+
+Human authentication is selected explicitly and independently from machine
+ingress:
+
+| Decision | Allowed values | Responsibility |
+|---|---|---|
+| `AZURE_AUTH_MODE` | `local`, `entra` | Exactly one human identity issuer |
+| `AZURE_MACHINE_ACCESS_MODE` | `none`, `gateway`, `direct` | How non-interactive callers reach the API |
+
+APIM and Entra remain independently optional. `local` must deploy without either.
+Missing, invalid, or contradictory human-auth configuration fails closed; Entra
+failure never falls back to local credentials.
+
+### Application boundary
+
+- Production always runs with RBAC enforcement enabled.
+- Every API operation requires a proved human or machine principal except health,
+  the non-secret auth-mode endpoint, and the local-mode login endpoint.
+- An Entra identity without a recognized application role receives 403 rather
+  than inheriting anonymous viewer access.
+- Local credentials use Argon2id hashes from one atomic Key Vault bundle. The
+  bundle also carries an RSA signing key, immutable account IDs, roles, enabled
+  state, and per-account token versions.
+- The API retrieves the latest bundle with its user-assigned managed identity.
+  No password, hash, credential document, or signing key is a Bicep parameter,
+  azd value, environment value, output, log entry, or committed file.
+- A bounded refresh makes password/role rotation and account revocation effective
+  without an application redeploy. A transient read/validation failure retains
+  one immutable last-known-good snapshot for a configured max-stale interval and
+  reports degraded health without secret data. After max-stale, local login and
+  token validation return 503 rather than authenticating indefinitely from stale
+  state.
+
+### Entra boundary
+
+- Container Apps Easy Auth manages the browser sign-in session.
+- Easy Auth requests a delegated API access-token scope and stores tokens.
+- nginx maps the validated `X-MS-TOKEN-AAD-ACCESS-TOKEN` to the API
+  `Authorization` header, then removes all `X-MS-*` headers.
+- The API independently validates issuer, audience, signature, expiry and
+  application role. It never trusts a platform principal header, including when
+  direct machine ingress is enabled.
+- The SPA explicitly begins `/.auth/login/aad`; Easy Auth allows the static shell
+  so API 401/403/502/503 responses remain observable and truthful.
+
+### Routing correction
+
+Every nginx API/docs/health proxy location uses the API FQDN for the HTTP `Host`
+header and TLS SNI. The incoming web hostname is retained only as
+`X-Forwarded-Host`. This removes the verified Container Apps route-back loop.
+
+### Credential lifecycle
+
+An explicit operator command, run only after infrastructure provision and only
+with separate authorization, prompts through `getpass` and writes directly to
+Key Vault through the Azure SDK. Bootstrap requires one enabled admin and creates
+no local plaintext artifact. Password/role changes increment that account's token
+version; disabling an account revokes it. JWTs carry a `kid`; normal signing-key
+rotation keeps one previous verification key until at least the maximum token
+lifetime, while explicit emergency revocation changes bundle generation and
+drops the old ring. Rollback republishes a validated prior document as a new
+latest version with a fresh generation/key ring, so revoked tokens cannot revive.
+
+### Deployment-path changes
+
+- Replace `AZURE_ENABLE_ENTRA_AUTH` with required `AZURE_AUTH_MODE`.
+- Thread the mode, Key Vault coordinates, API audience/scope and auth settings
+  through `main.bicep`, `platform.bicep`, and `container-apps.bicep`.
+- Emit `RBAC_ENABLED=true` and only the non-secret coordinates appropriate to the
+  selected mode.
+- Add a predeploy metadata check for an enabled local-auth secret version. It must
+  not retrieve the secret value.
+- Keep the existing API identity's Key Vault read grant; do not grant the web app
+  access to the local-auth bundle.
+- Update nginx, SPA bootstrap/sign-out, API auth, operator scripts, docs and tests
+  as one coherent change.
+
+### Migration and rollback
+
+- The plaintext `.local-accounts.txt` format and `LOCAL_ACCOUNTS_ENABLED` switch
+  are retired and explicitly rejected.
+- Existing local tokens require sign-in again because new tokens bind to bundle
+  generation and account token version.
+- Entra deployments must provide an API audience and delegated scope; omission
+  does not select local mode.
+- Business data and database schemas are unchanged.
+- Application rollback is a Container Apps revision traffic rollback after a
+  compatible auth configuration is restored. Credential rollback creates a new
+  latest Key Vault version as described above.
+
+### Implementation validation
+
+- [x] Settings and auth-mode matrix, including missing/invalid/cross-mode refusal
+- [x] Argon2id bundle schema, admin invariant, size bound and uniform verification
+- [x] Token generation/version revocation, bounded `kid` overlap, degraded
+      max-stale refresh and post-max-stale refusal
+- [x] Anonymous production refusal, real role enforcement and machine-key isolation
+- [x] Local/Entra SPA bootstrap, sign-out and truthful error matrix
+- [x] nginx Host/SNI and reserved-header forwarding guards
+- [x] Bicep build/lint and compiled-template mode/secret/RBAC assertions
+- [x] PowerShell syntax and metadata-only predeploy checks
+- [x] Targeted backend/frontend tests, typecheck and production web build
+- [x] Final diff and secret-pattern inspection
+
+### Validation evidence
+
+- Focused backend/IaC/security suite: 69 passed.
+- Frontend auth/equivalent-fetch suite: 93 passed.
+- Full frontend suite in four bounded shards: 146 files, 1,821 tests, zero
+  failures. The unsharded worker pool timed out under known resource contention;
+  one-worker execution also hung, so shards are the complete-suite evidence.
+- Frontend lint exits zero with existing Fast Refresh/hook warnings; TypeScript
+  and production Vite build succeed.
+- `az bicep build --file infra/main.bicep --stdout` succeeds. Two existing BCP422
+  conditional-key warnings remain in `key-vault-secrets.bicep`; this change
+  neither introduced nor widened them.
+- All modified PowerShell scripts parse as script blocks.
+- Final specialist security review reports no vulnerabilities after narrowing the
+  Entra token-store SAS to one private Blob container and enforcing the operator
+  password floor.
+- Exact final default backend unit run: 4,975 passed, 21 skipped, 9 failed. All nine
+  are in two untouched reviewer fixtures that read ambient AI configuration from
+  `routers/ai.py`; their exact selector passes 9/9 with complete synthetic,
+  process-only AI settings and no network call. This is an inherited
+  order/environment-dependent test defect, not reported as a green default suite.
+- No Azure, Key Vault, deployment, database migration, credential bootstrap,
+  secret read/write, or real credential generation was performed.
+
+### Static role verification
+
+- API user-assigned identity retains `Key Vault Secrets User` at the deployment
+  vault, which is required for runtime local-bundle reads; no write role is
+  granted to the workload.
+- Web identity remains limited to the Entra client-secret resource. It receives
+  no access to the local-auth bundle, database credentials, or machine key.
+- API/web identities retain resource-scoped `AcrPull`; API retains the existing
+  OpenAI/Search data-plane roles in identity mode.
+- The Entra token store uses a container-scoped 90-day service SAS held as a
+  secure Container Apps secret, not an additional workload role or root output.
+
+### Azure Validate boundary
+
+Offline recipe checks are complete. `azd provision --preview`, ARM subscription
+validation/what-if, Azure Policy evaluation, live role verification, and
+`PreDeploy.ps1` execution are deliberately deferred: they invoke the selected
+azd environment and/or live Azure metadata, while this authorization permits no
+live deployment workflow or credential bootstrap. The status remains **Ready for
+Validation**, not `Validated`, until those separately authorized checks pass.
+
+### Remaining containment and external prerequisites
+
+- Local mode is intentionally constrained to one API replica. Its in-memory
+  limiter resets on restart; horizontal scale requires shared transactional
+  attempt/lockout state.
+- Entra mode requires an externally configured v2 API app registration, delegated
+  scope, application roles/user assignment, client credential, and consent.
+- The Entra Blob token-store service SAS expires after 90 days and must be rotated
+  with the auth configuration before expiry.
+- Deployment and real local-auth bundle bootstrap remain separately authorized
+  operational actions.
+
+### Execution gate
+
+Repository implementation and offline validation are approved. Azure deployment,
+Key Vault access, secret creation, credential bootstrap, database migration,
+commit, push, merge, reset, stash and clean remain out of scope.
